<article class="env-definition" id="0BDS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BDS">Definition <span data-tag="0BDS">5.28.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $I$ be a set and for $i \in I$ let $E_ i \subset X$ be a subset. We say the collection $\{ E_ i\} _{i \in I}$ is <em>locally finite</em> if for all $x \in X$ there exists an open neighbourhood $U$ of $x$ such that $\{ i \in I | E_ i \cap U \not= \emptyset \} $ is finite. </p>
